@template gruff
// ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.3 item 26: crew comment when you wear dirty clothes. clothes.remark: yesterday's clothes
// (flag:clothes.stale); clothes.grubby: a grubby uniform (flag:clothes.grubby, AC3). Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
// Kind, never mean: the joke is on the clothes, not on you.
== clothes.remark
? flag:clothes.stale
- Hm. Yesterday's shirt.
- Change that. Then we'll talk.
? flag:clothes.stale tier>=friend
- Laundry. Today. You'll thank me.   #warm
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- Hm. Filthy. Good work, then. Change.
- You're dripping grime. Not on my floor.   #funny
? flag:clothes.grubby tier>=friend
- Clean up. You did well. Still filthy.   #warm

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more lines for the chat card's opener (greet, near), so a tap doesn't repeat.
// Heard after a person's own lines are used up (FX13's no-repeat). {hi}, {nick} and {me} are the speaker's own words.
== greet
- Hm. You.
- {hi}. What is it?
- {hi}. Make it quick.
- You again. Fine.
- Hm. Still standing? Good.
- {hi}. Don't just stand there.
- {hi}. Something on your mind?
- What. Oh. It's you. Fine.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. You'll do.
- Hm. You've been working. I can tell.
? time:morning
- Morning. Coffee first. Then words.
? time:evening
- Evening. Long day. Yours too, by the look.
== near
- Busy. Talk if you must.
- Hold that. No. Like that.
- {room}. Somebody has to.
- Don't watch me. Do something.
- Nearly done. Wait.
- It's fine. It'll hold.
- I'm working. Speak up.
- Hm. Not bad, this. Don't tell anyone.
